WEBVTT

00:00:01.980 --> 00:00:04.690
Kazuma, vowing victory at the newcomers’ battle,

00:00:04.690 --> 00:00:07.520
obtained a secret weapon for that purpose.

00:00:08.150 --> 00:00:12.710
And then, he went to face the day
of the newcomers’ battle finals.

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:15.580
Azuma Kazuma!

00:00:15.580 --> 00:00:17.950
For being 5 minutes late,
minus 5 points!

00:00:17.950 --> 00:00:19.410
What?!

00:00:22.130 --> 00:00:24.420
There’s English bread, German bread, and French bread,

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:26.300
but Japan’s bread, <i>Japan</i>, does not exist.

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:28.590
In that case, there’s no choice but to create it.

00:00:28.590 --> 00:00:31.990
This story is a serious, biographical ballad of a boy who possesses Solar Hands,

00:00:31.990 --> 00:00:37.220
Azuma Kazuma, who will create a Japanese bread made by and for the Japanese people,

00:00:37.220 --> 00:00:40.820
which can be presented to the world proudly.

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:54.530
Somewhere far away, there are people listening carefully.

00:00:54.530 --> 00:00:58.120
Yakitate!! Japan
Somewhere far away, there are people listening carefully.

00:00:58.120 --> 00:00:59.450
Yakitate!! Japan

00:00:59.450 --> 00:01:06.090
In every place, there are people looking up at the sky.

00:01:07.210 --> 00:01:13.920
Under the night sky, we, who are whistling...

00:01:15.010 --> 00:01:21.680
without words, are just tracing constellations with our fingers.

00:01:21.930 --> 00:01:29.150
The dreams of the cold-sensitive... Your cold hands...

00:01:30.150 --> 00:01:38.530
The warming magic is to believe in one path.

00:01:38.950 --> 00:01:47.290
The single star found on the other side of the comet cloud...

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:51.550
whether it be a shining or a faint star...

00:01:51.760 --> 00:01:54.510
is the light of only you.

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:58.290
On the other side of the cloud in your heart,

00:01:58.290 --> 00:02:03.100
is a sign post that remains unseen.

00:02:03.560 --> 00:02:10.820
Now, opening these hands, what will you believe in today?

00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:14.490
Garbage and trash!!

00:02:14.490 --> 00:02:16.710
Kazuma selected the worst possible butter!

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:21.490
I’ve done it once again...

00:02:22.120 --> 00:02:24.370
Is what I’d like to say, but...

00:02:24.370 --> 00:02:26.500
this time, we’re not using a system of point reductions.

00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:31.510
I think that it is regrettable, but
it’s a lifesaver for you, right?

00:02:31.510 --> 00:02:33.010
What the...

00:02:33.010 --> 00:02:35.800
Quit frightening me like that
will ya, old man Kuroyanagi.

00:02:35.800 --> 00:02:36.840
However!

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:38.850
I am still 22 years old!

00:02:38.850 --> 00:02:41.180
I am telling you that I am not an old man!

00:02:41.180 --> 00:02:44.520
If you say if once more, I’ll have you permanently banned from this industry!

00:02:44.520 --> 00:02:45.770
Make sure to remember that!

00:02:46.940 --> 00:02:48.270
Permanently banned?

00:02:50.070 --> 00:02:52.030
Well then...
I shall start with the explanations once again.

00:02:52.030 --> 00:02:54.280
The finals consist of 16 participants from the A block

00:02:54.280 --> 00:02:55.650
and 16 participants from the B block.

00:02:55.650 --> 00:02:59.710
We will have the 32 finals participants fight
for the championship in a tournament system.

00:03:01.240 --> 00:03:04.450
However, 58 people have passed
the preliminaries this time.

00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:07.540
More than the expected number of people have passed.

00:03:07.540 --> 00:03:09.750
Therefore, we will have another set of preliminaries.

00:03:12.800 --> 00:03:15.470
Of the 58 candidates,
we shall have 32 remaining.

00:03:15.470 --> 00:03:17.380
And the topic for the second preliminaries is...

00:03:17.380 --> 00:03:18.210
Hang on there for just a minute!
And the topic for the second preliminaries is...

00:03:18.210 --> 00:03:18.970
Hang on there for just a minute!

00:03:24.180 --> 00:03:25.550
What is it with all of you?

00:03:26.430 --> 00:03:29.310
I’m Umino Katsuo of the Tsugaru branch.
Note: Tsugaru is an area in the Aomori prefecture up north.

00:03:29.310 --> 00:03:31.310
He looks like...

00:03:32.070 --> 00:03:33.940
Unable to agree with the results of the preliminaries,

00:03:33.940 --> 00:03:36.280
I’ve come all the way from Aomori.

00:03:36.280 --> 00:03:38.110
These people here are also people

00:03:38.110 --> 00:03:40.570
who aren’t satisfied with the results of the preliminaries.

00:03:40.990 --> 00:03:41.950
Exactly!

00:03:41.950 --> 00:03:45.070
With just this single slip of paper,
asking us to be satisfied is ridiculous!

00:03:45.570 --> 00:03:45.700
Baldly!!
Results
You've failed!

00:03:45.700 --> 00:03:47.570
And I’m not even bald...
Baldly!!
Results
You've failed!

00:03:47.570 --> 00:03:47.580
And I’m not even bald...

00:03:48.920 --> 00:03:51.170
Yeah, that really is a cruel method of communication...

00:03:51.170 --> 00:03:53.210
but it’s consistent with Kuroyanagi’s character.

00:03:53.210 --> 00:03:56.920
Oh, the trash is not satisfied, eh?

00:03:56.920 --> 00:03:58.300
Don’t make me laugh!

00:03:58.300 --> 00:03:59.800
In that case, you may see it!

00:03:59.800 --> 00:04:05.140
This is the disqualified result of
what you trash have produced!

00:04:19.530 --> 00:04:20.870
Can this be...?

00:04:21.320 --> 00:04:23.580
You said that you were Umino Katsuo, right?

00:04:23.580 --> 00:04:26.540
Come to think of it, I remember your bread really well.

00:04:26.540 --> 00:04:28.870
Because, at the grading stage of the bread,
it was that bread which left me...

00:04:30.500 --> 00:04:31.510
Disgusting!

00:04:32.420 --> 00:04:35.970
with the memory of the most unpleasant
bread I’d ever tasted.

00:04:36.840 --> 00:04:39.970
Making bread with vinegar, without
considering the taste...

00:04:39.970 --> 00:04:42.590
This attitude of thinking only of clearing the topic is...

00:04:42.590 --> 00:04:44.220
the first piece of evidence
of you being trash.

00:04:44.220 --> 00:04:45.220
Also!

00:04:45.810 --> 00:04:50.560
Naturally, if you’re using a highly volatile
ingredient like vinegar or alcohol,

00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:53.190
then the rectangular dinner bread
made using a lid is expected.

00:04:53.190 --> 00:04:55.350
However, the bread you made was

00:04:56.230 --> 00:04:58.780
a mountain-shaped bread that forms
by rising when no lid is used.

00:04:58.780 --> 00:05:00.900
The percentage of vinegar decreases during preparation,

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:02.570
leading to a reduction of the anti-microbial effect...

00:05:02.570 --> 00:05:04.240
Therefore, mold grew on it as well!

00:05:04.240 --> 00:05:06.200
That is the second piece of evidence of you being trash.

00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:08.500
You, holding two pieces of evidence
of being trash, are...

00:05:08.500 --> 00:05:10.040
trash amongst trash.

00:05:10.040 --> 00:05:11.540
Royalty amongst trash.

00:05:11.540 --> 00:05:13.120
the King of Trash!

00:05:13.290 --> 00:05:15.500
Gan

00:05:16.800 --> 00:05:19.090
Those who are still left with any
objections, step forward!

00:05:19.720 --> 00:05:21.590
I’ll tell you exactly why you were disqualified.

00:05:22.260 --> 00:05:25.260
Old man Kuroyanagi’s being his
usual, severe self, isn’t he?

00:05:25.260 --> 00:05:26.340
I mean, Mister...

00:05:27.310 --> 00:05:28.640
Isn’t it all right?

00:05:28.640 --> 00:05:30.430
To let them take the exam
once again, that is.

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:31.060
What?

00:05:31.560 --> 00:05:34.560
This fellow seems to have come all the
way here from a considerable distance,

00:05:34.560 --> 00:05:38.530
and I think the very fact that they’ve come
here shows that they have guts.

00:05:38.530 --> 00:05:40.940
Allowing them to take the exam
just once more wouldn’t be...

00:05:40.940 --> 00:05:42.320
Don’t kid around!

00:05:42.320 --> 00:05:45.200
In what world would you find an
examiner who says “right, right”

00:05:45.200 --> 00:05:47.040
to guts, and overturns examination results?

00:05:48.740 --> 00:05:50.820
I understand that I’m trash.

00:05:52.160 --> 00:05:55.470
But give me just one more chance.

00:05:56.250 --> 00:05:58.430
I’ll do anything.

00:06:01.550 --> 00:06:02.760
This is annoying.

00:06:02.760 --> 00:06:04.590
Throw out this trash!

00:06:04.970 --> 00:06:06.890
Please!

00:06:06.890 --> 00:06:08.980
Just once more!

00:06:10.220 --> 00:06:12.970
I can’t return home like this.

00:06:13.310 --> 00:06:15.470
I’ll do anything!

00:06:16.230 --> 00:06:17.640
Hey, come on!

00:06:18.730 --> 00:06:22.360
Amazing. He’s really got
some amazing guts.

00:06:22.360 --> 00:06:23.570
What in the world...?

00:06:23.570 --> 00:06:25.030
Quiet down there, will ya?

00:06:27.070 --> 00:06:29.160
Umino Katsuo, and the three others.

00:06:29.160 --> 00:06:31.870
If you go so far as to say all that,
then show us your determination!

00:06:35.790 --> 00:06:36.920
Any one of you is fine.

00:06:36.920 --> 00:06:38.250
Let’s see you eat that trashy bread.

00:06:41.760 --> 00:06:44.000
If you can do that, I’ll think about it.

00:06:44.720 --> 00:06:46.510
Like we could do something like that!

00:06:46.510 --> 00:06:49.180
If we ate something like that, what we’d get
wouldn’t end with just an upset stomach...

00:06:49.180 --> 00:06:50.470
It’s unreasonable...

00:06:50.470 --> 00:06:51.890
If you can’t do it, then leave!

00:06:51.890 --> 00:06:54.010
It’s the obvious outcome
of the exam results.

00:06:55.140 --> 00:06:56.770
That’s too cruel.

00:06:56.770 --> 00:06:58.480
He’s a demon... A black demon!

00:07:02.940 --> 00:07:05.530
Certainly, it’s just as the examiner says.

00:07:05.530 --> 00:07:08.610
I didn’t think enough, so...

00:07:08.990 --> 00:07:12.570
I ended up making... trashy bread.

00:07:22.210 --> 00:07:23.300
This is it!

00:07:23.300 --> 00:07:26.800
This is the moldy bread that I made.

00:07:28.180 --> 00:07:31.970
He could identify his own bread by its smell...

00:07:31.970 --> 00:07:33.510
His nose is...

00:07:41.770 --> 00:07:45.280
D-Don’t tell me he seriously intends to eat it...

00:07:46.280 --> 00:07:48.900
Mommy!

00:07:51.450 --> 00:07:52.370
That’s enough!

00:07:52.370 --> 00:07:53.670
Stop it.

00:07:54.410 --> 00:07:57.000
This should be enough, right?
Mister Kuroyanagi?

00:07:57.000 --> 00:07:58.920
M-Mister?

00:07:58.920 --> 00:08:01.000
He was seriously going to eat it.

00:08:01.000 --> 00:08:03.250
That determination is impressive, isn’t it?

00:08:03.250 --> 00:08:05.340
Either way, you’re going to do
another preliminary, right?

00:08:05.340 --> 00:08:06.880
Just one more chance should be fine, shouldn’t it?

00:08:06.880 --> 00:08:08.470
Azuma Kazuma!

00:08:08.470 --> 00:08:09.800
You...

00:08:09.800 --> 00:08:13.220
You, a mere existence of a latecomer, dare
to state an opinion to me, Kuroyanagi?

00:08:16.730 --> 00:08:18.190
Shouldn’t it be all right?

00:08:18.190 --> 00:08:20.110
Give him one more chance.

00:08:22.520 --> 00:08:23.940
Meister Kirisaki...

00:08:23.940 --> 00:08:24.440
flour milling

00:08:24.440 --> 00:08:27.190
could not possibly be here!
flour milling

00:08:28.150 --> 00:08:29.450
Um... Manager...

00:08:29.450 --> 00:08:31.150
It’s quite obviously not him, so...

00:08:32.780 --> 00:08:35.080
The craftsmanship was perfect, but...

00:08:35.080 --> 00:08:37.660
No, the problem must be
my stubble, right?

00:08:37.660 --> 00:08:38.660
Whatever...

00:08:39.290 --> 00:08:40.370
Oh well, it’s like...

00:08:40.370 --> 00:08:42.880
I didn’t think that you’d listen to
what I’d say anymore, so...

00:08:42.880 --> 00:08:43.670
Of course!

00:08:44.710 --> 00:08:48.170
As far as I’m concerned, you and I
were finished two years ago.

00:08:48.170 --> 00:08:50.630
It’s troublesome for you to continue
to consider me your student.

00:08:50.630 --> 00:08:51.720
Kuroyanagi,

00:08:51.720 --> 00:08:53.720
have you forgotten?

00:08:54.390 --> 00:08:57.140
The most important thing as a baker.

00:08:57.640 --> 00:08:58.220
What?

00:08:59.730 --> 00:09:01.110
It’s your heart.

00:09:03.230 --> 00:09:06.350
The most important things for us bakers...

00:09:07.280 --> 00:09:10.610
are the heart, passion, guts, and fighting spirit!

00:09:11.360 --> 00:09:13.160
Isn’t it enough?

00:09:13.160 --> 00:09:15.660
That boy has a good heart.

00:09:15.660 --> 00:09:18.120
You’ve forgotten even that, haven’t you?

00:09:18.120 --> 00:09:19.590
Kuroyanagi?

00:09:21.790 --> 00:09:24.540
Kuroyanagi, try and remember.

00:09:24.540 --> 00:09:28.680
Weren’t you once in a situation like that little boy’s?

00:09:29.170 --> 00:09:30.260
Wha...

00:09:30.260 --> 00:09:32.130
Please wait!

00:09:32.130 --> 00:09:34.220
Matsushiro-senpai!!
Note: “Senpai” is a way of addressing an upperclassman.

00:09:34.220 --> 00:09:36.850
I beg you. Please!

00:09:36.850 --> 00:09:40.350
Please make me a student of yours!

00:09:40.350 --> 00:09:41.230
All right.
Please make me a student of yours!

00:09:43.980 --> 00:09:46.650
I wonder if I should expose it?
You, squirming, down on your knees...

00:09:46.650 --> 00:09:49.110
Are you blackmailing me?

00:09:49.110 --> 00:09:51.160
You, squirming, down on your knees...

00:09:55.530 --> 00:09:56.620
You, boy over there!

00:09:56.620 --> 00:09:58.120
I’m telling you that in recognition of your guts,

00:09:58.120 --> 00:10:01.080
you are given the right to take
part in the second preliminary.

00:10:01.660 --> 00:10:04.010
This should do, right, Matsushiro!

00:10:05.880 --> 00:10:07.180
That will be fine.

00:10:07.880 --> 00:10:11.810
It would be a waste to lose his
strength at such an early point.

00:10:14.680 --> 00:10:16.560
Thank goodness, right?

00:10:18.930 --> 00:10:20.860
Ah, sorry, sorry.

00:10:21.730 --> 00:10:23.810
Thank you very much.

00:10:23.810 --> 00:10:25.060
Don’t worry about it.

00:10:25.850 --> 00:10:29.070
But, why did you help me?

00:10:31.280 --> 00:10:35.000
Because you look a lot like the pig,
Sanpi, that we keep at home.

00:10:45.540 --> 00:10:47.920
I can’t think of you as a stranger.

00:10:47.920 --> 00:10:49.800
I really can’t like that reason...

00:10:50.880 --> 00:10:52.750
Don’t worry about it.

00:10:54.050 --> 00:10:56.390
However, that boy even

00:10:56.390 --> 00:10:58.800
surprised me with his fierce spirit...

00:10:58.800 --> 00:11:00.260
There was an unnecessary interruption.

00:11:01.010 --> 00:11:04.560
We will begin the second preliminary now, as planned.

00:11:04.560 --> 00:11:06.650
The topic for the second preliminary is...

00:11:06.650 --> 00:11:07.980
butter rolls!

00:11:07.980 --> 00:11:11.070
We will have 32 left out of the 59.

00:11:11.070 --> 00:11:12.520
The time limit is 3 hours.

00:11:12.900 --> 00:11:15.330
That’s really dull, isn’t it?

00:11:18.120 --> 00:11:20.200
Shut up!!

00:11:20.200 --> 00:11:23.460
You trash who don’t understand
the value of a butter roll!

00:11:24.080 --> 00:11:25.960
All right, listen carefully...

00:11:25.960 --> 00:11:29.250
There are over 20,000 primary schools all over Japan.

00:11:29.250 --> 00:11:32.000
School lunches are considered to be a model meal.

00:11:32.000 --> 00:11:34.550
Within that, the butter roll, being a standard food item,

00:11:34.550 --> 00:11:37.510
is always included in the menu once a month.

00:11:37.510 --> 00:11:40.680
It’s the king of Japanese school lunches, so to speak!

00:11:40.680 --> 00:11:42.470
I’m the King-roll.

00:11:43.020 --> 00:11:47.600
Even within the Pantasia group, it’s amongst
the 10 most profitable breads.

00:11:47.600 --> 00:11:48.930
In other words,

00:11:49.440 --> 00:11:52.230
it’s a bread that trash, newcomer
bakers like you should be calling

00:11:52.230 --> 00:11:54.990
Lord Butter Roll!

00:11:54.990 --> 00:11:57.240
Do you understand, you trash?!

00:11:57.240 --> 00:11:59.940
L-Lord Butter R-R-Roll?!

00:12:07.040 --> 00:12:10.290
Here, we have set out what can be
called the lifeline of the butter roll.

00:12:10.290 --> 00:12:13.340
From A to H, there are 8 different
varieties of butter set out here.

00:12:13.920 --> 00:12:16.760
It ranges from the world’s best butter

00:12:16.760 --> 00:12:18.930
to regular home consumption butter.

00:12:18.930 --> 00:12:20.800
It doesn’t matter which you use, but...

00:12:20.800 --> 00:12:25.180
Anyhow, the top 32 to make a delicious
butter roll will be selected.

00:12:26.100 --> 00:12:28.440
However, sampling the butter is prohibited.

00:12:28.440 --> 00:12:30.230
We don’t need a baker in the main branch

00:12:30.230 --> 00:12:32.270
who can’t determine the quality
of butter without having to

00:12:32.270 --> 00:12:34.020
taste them, one by one.

00:12:34.020 --> 00:12:37.240
What butter you use, according to your judgment and knowledge,

00:12:37.240 --> 00:12:39.660
will determine the results of this preliminary.

00:12:39.660 --> 00:12:40.400
Azuma-san...

00:12:40.990 --> 00:12:42.660
what’s this?

00:12:42.660 --> 00:12:44.120
My secret weapon.

00:12:44.120 --> 00:12:45.450
Tsukino, take care of it for me.

00:12:45.450 --> 00:12:48.080
Eh? Secret weapon?

00:12:52.880 --> 00:12:53.460
Hey!

00:12:55.380 --> 00:12:57.010
What should I do?

00:12:58.300 --> 00:13:01.260
Main Branch employees are exempt from preliminaries.

00:13:01.260 --> 00:13:04.260
You are automatically included in the 32.

00:13:04.260 --> 00:13:05.810
Just observe or something.

00:13:05.810 --> 00:13:06.560
Observe?

00:13:10.060 --> 00:13:11.230
All right.

00:13:11.230 --> 00:13:15.560
It’s not a bad idea to just see how
far those two have matured.

00:13:16.280 --> 00:13:18.570
All of them appear to be the same butter.

00:13:18.570 --> 00:13:20.320
What can possibly be different?

00:13:20.990 --> 00:13:23.870
Certainly, if you can’t taste it,

00:13:23.870 --> 00:13:26.200
then the criteria for judgment
would be color and such...

00:13:26.200 --> 00:13:27.630
In other words, its external appearance.

00:13:28.830 --> 00:13:30.160
In that respect,

00:13:30.160 --> 00:13:32.040
they’re all pretty similar.

00:13:32.040 --> 00:13:33.750
I can’t be careless here.

00:13:35.960 --> 00:13:38.100
I don’t really understand, anyway...

00:13:39.800 --> 00:13:41.050
Okay, then... C!

00:13:41.050 --> 00:13:42.510
I’ll just go with the C butter.

00:13:42.510 --> 00:13:43.470
Give me that one.

00:13:43.470 --> 00:13:44.600
What?

00:13:44.600 --> 00:13:46.300
“Just go with,” he says...

00:13:47.220 --> 00:13:49.180
Azuma Kazuma.

00:13:49.180 --> 00:13:50.810
To think that you’d select C...

00:13:50.810 --> 00:13:52.810
You fool!

00:13:52.810 --> 00:13:54.610
With this, you’re done for as well.

00:13:54.610 --> 00:13:56.860
That which you have chosen is...

00:14:06.530 --> 00:14:08.490
Who is he?

00:14:08.490 --> 00:14:10.450
He selected it, just like that...

00:14:10.450 --> 00:14:12.540
Is that an amazing butter?

00:14:12.540 --> 00:14:15.420
He said something like
“I don’t understand, anyway...”

00:14:15.420 --> 00:14:20.090
No! Saying that is a plan, so that we don’t copy him!

00:14:20.090 --> 00:14:21.090
What?

00:14:21.090 --> 00:14:23.420
I just remembered,
because of that hairband...

00:14:23.970 --> 00:14:26.350
At the St. Pierre new product competition,

00:14:26.350 --> 00:14:28.800
he was the fellow who came to a draw
with the manager Mokoyama.

00:14:28.800 --> 00:14:30.350
The one that was on television?

00:14:30.350 --> 00:14:34.060
So that means, undoubtedly,
that he’s considerably skillful.

00:14:37.400 --> 00:14:38.940
I’ll have C, too.

00:14:38.940 --> 00:14:39.480
Me, too.

00:14:39.480 --> 00:14:40.400
For me as well!

00:14:40.400 --> 00:14:41.020
C for me.

00:14:41.020 --> 00:14:41.860
C, please.

00:14:41.860 --> 00:14:42.860
Oh my...

00:14:42.860 --> 00:14:46.910
Led by Kazuma, a lot of people are going for C, but...

00:14:46.910 --> 00:14:50.210
is it really that good a butter?

00:14:50.740 --> 00:14:52.800
Probably not, right?

00:14:57.080 --> 00:14:59.880
Azuma is not the kind to lie.

00:14:59.880 --> 00:15:03.670
If he says, “I don’t understand, anyway,”
he probably really doesn’t know.

00:15:03.670 --> 00:15:06.220
Well, if the number of competitors
reduces quickly in this way...

00:15:06.220 --> 00:15:08.640
it’s good for me, as it makes things easier, but...

00:15:15.520 --> 00:15:16.940
What an idiot.

00:15:16.940 --> 00:15:18.690
He’s not an animal,

00:15:18.690 --> 00:15:21.850
so he can’t possibly figure out the
butter by something like smell...

00:15:22.190 --> 00:15:23.480
I’d like A.

00:15:23.480 --> 00:15:25.240
W-What?

00:15:26.410 --> 00:15:28.490
What’s with this confidence?

00:15:28.490 --> 00:15:30.280
Did he really figure it out by its smell?

00:15:34.250 --> 00:15:37.920
A is the world’s best butter,
Echire butter.

00:15:38.540 --> 00:15:41.210
It certainly is a fragrant butter,

00:15:41.210 --> 00:15:43.290
but to be able to discern that by smell...

00:15:44.720 --> 00:15:47.130
In France, while looking for truffles in the mountains,

00:15:47.130 --> 00:15:48.680
they are said to use pigs...

00:15:49.720 --> 00:15:51.690
He’s really like that, isn’t he?

00:15:52.640 --> 00:15:54.470
The fearful, pig-snouted man!

00:15:58.520 --> 00:16:01.850
Almost everyone has chosen a butter.

00:16:02.610 --> 00:16:05.650
Azuma’s already kneading the dough, is he?

00:16:05.650 --> 00:16:07.360
Well, there is a time limit, so...

00:16:07.360 --> 00:16:09.530
I should also decide soon, or else...

00:16:09.530 --> 00:16:12.450
For now, that “snort snort” fellow seemed confident,

00:16:12.450 --> 00:16:13.860
so let’s go with A...

00:16:15.000 --> 00:16:18.250
This is already melting from the heat of the lights.

00:16:18.250 --> 00:16:22.410
It’s like it’s mocking me for being
indecisive for so long...

00:16:22.410 --> 00:16:26.380
Oh well... after having waited for so long,
all the other butters must have also...

00:16:26.970 --> 00:16:27.960
W-What the...?

00:16:28.760 --> 00:16:31.010
The G butter hasn’t melted at all.

00:16:32.390 --> 00:16:34.810
I see... I’ve got it!

00:16:34.810 --> 00:16:36.470
This is it... this is it!

00:16:37.390 --> 00:16:39.440
It’s G. I’ll have G.

00:16:40.150 --> 00:16:43.940
Huh? Kawachi chose the G butter, did he?

00:16:43.940 --> 00:16:46.150
That’s butter with low water content.

00:16:46.150 --> 00:16:47.990
Just as the name implies,

00:16:47.990 --> 00:16:51.320
it has an overwhelmingly lower water
content than other butters, and thus,

00:16:51.320 --> 00:16:53.410
the taste of the bread is not overpowered and...

00:16:53.410 --> 00:16:57.330
the weak point of the butter roll,
its stickiness, is reduced.

00:16:57.330 --> 00:17:01.910
In a way, it’s more suitable for the
butter roll than the Echire butter.

00:17:02.840 --> 00:17:07.170
He seems to have matured a little since
that time, hasn’t he... Kawachi.

00:17:07.170 --> 00:17:08.420
At any rate...

00:17:09.010 --> 00:17:10.880
Azuma Kazuma,

00:17:10.880 --> 00:17:13.300
I’m disappointed in you.

00:17:13.300 --> 00:17:15.010
Even within A-H,

00:17:15.010 --> 00:17:17.090
the one you chose is trash.

00:17:19.180 --> 00:17:22.700
It’s a thing that can’t even be called butter.

00:17:24.060 --> 00:17:26.280
Following Azuma,

00:17:26.280 --> 00:17:30.360
the people who chose C will almost entirely fail.

00:17:31.530 --> 00:17:33.370
I’m sorry, Suwabara...

00:17:33.370 --> 00:17:35.120
but one of your goals

00:17:35.120 --> 00:17:37.240
seems like he won’t even make it past the preliminaries.

00:17:41.080 --> 00:17:44.790
Azuma-san seems to be proceeding
at a fairly high pace.

00:17:44.790 --> 00:17:46.420
I wonder if it’s okay...

00:17:46.420 --> 00:17:49.430
At this rate, it’s probably bad.

00:17:49.970 --> 00:17:51.010
Bad?

00:17:51.010 --> 00:17:54.770
His butter roll has a fatal deficiency.

00:17:55.300 --> 00:17:57.150
A fatal deficiency?

00:17:58.140 --> 00:17:59.640
Azuma Kazuma,

00:17:59.640 --> 00:18:01.020
learn from this.

00:18:01.020 --> 00:18:02.430
How very fragile you are...

00:18:03.350 --> 00:18:04.690
Until now,

00:18:04.690 --> 00:18:07.780
your genius-like talent, and the
things you were blessed with,

00:18:07.780 --> 00:18:10.440
probably supported you as a baker.

00:18:11.200 --> 00:18:12.280
However,

00:18:12.280 --> 00:18:15.940
there’s one definitive trait that you lack as a baker.

00:18:15.940 --> 00:18:18.410
That is... the knowledge required of a baker.

00:18:19.910 --> 00:18:24.540
No matter how much of a talent
you’ve been blessed with,

00:18:24.540 --> 00:18:27.670
if you don’t have the knowledge required of a baker,

00:18:27.670 --> 00:18:30.460
and haven’t worked extremely hard, you
can’t possibly make a delicious bread.

00:18:30.460 --> 00:18:31.470
It’s done!

00:18:31.470 --> 00:18:33.550
W-W-What?!

00:18:33.550 --> 00:18:34.930
It’s done already?

00:18:34.930 --> 00:18:37.510
What?
He’s already done baking it?

00:18:42.180 --> 00:18:43.510
It smells good.

00:18:44.600 --> 00:18:46.430
Oh, I see... that’s how he did it, eh?

00:18:50.320 --> 00:18:52.030
What does this mean?

00:18:52.030 --> 00:18:55.700
Baking a butter roll normally takes
15 minutes in its entirety.

00:18:55.700 --> 00:18:56.780
However...

00:18:56.780 --> 00:19:01.200
Azuma placed the dough in the
oven only 3 minutes ago.

00:19:01.200 --> 00:19:03.620
Having noticed your failure in choosing the butter,

00:19:03.620 --> 00:19:07.880
have you decided to forfeit this challenge, as you
couldn’t possibly have any prospects for victory?

00:19:16.340 --> 00:19:18.470
Have you realized your worthlessness on your own?

00:19:26.100 --> 00:19:28.600
It’s really fragrant. Perfect.

00:19:28.600 --> 00:19:31.230
Yeah, my butter roll really is the best.

00:19:31.230 --> 00:19:33.690
What?!

00:19:33.690 --> 00:19:38.320
But it seems to have a vaguely different
fragrance from the usual.

00:19:38.320 --> 00:19:40.240
Oh well, it’s all right.

00:19:40.700 --> 00:19:43.700
Hey, Ol... Mister Kuroyanagi.

00:19:43.700 --> 00:19:46.330
It’s done already, so... I’ll leave you to the sampling.

00:19:46.330 --> 00:19:47.460
Not possible, not possible.

00:19:47.460 --> 00:19:50.210
I will do the judging after everyone is done.

00:19:50.210 --> 00:19:51.380
Wait.

00:19:51.380 --> 00:19:53.100
Is that so?

00:19:53.550 --> 00:19:54.250
Oh well...

00:19:55.760 --> 00:19:57.930
After using the absolute worst C butter,

00:19:57.930 --> 00:20:01.760
there is absolutely no way that you
can make a delicious butter roll.

00:20:01.760 --> 00:20:03.890
You may have thought that making me sample it while

00:20:03.890 --> 00:20:06.890
it was still freshly baked would
cover up the taste a little...

00:20:06.890 --> 00:20:08.850
But that’s not going to happen.

00:20:08.850 --> 00:20:12.900
Winning or losing here is 100% determined
right when you choose the butter.

00:20:12.900 --> 00:20:15.270
However much you flail about, you’re going to fail.

00:20:38.050 --> 00:20:38.930
Time is up.

00:20:38.930 --> 00:20:41.300
All right, then. I’ll announce the people
who’ve passed at this point.

00:20:41.300 --> 00:20:43.010
Huh? What about sampling them?

00:20:43.010 --> 00:20:43.680
This can’t be, can it?

00:20:43.680 --> 00:20:45.340
What’s happening?
This can’t be, can it?

00:20:46.180 --> 00:20:50.310
First, the 16 participants who chose G,
the butter with low water content...

00:20:50.310 --> 00:20:51.900
That’s me.

00:20:51.900 --> 00:20:56.360
Congratulations on finding the most suitable,
low water content butter for a butter roll.

00:20:56.360 --> 00:20:58.030
There’s no need to even taste them.

00:20:58.030 --> 00:20:59.230
You’ve all passed.

00:20:59.740 --> 00:21:00.910
All right!

00:21:00.910 --> 00:21:01.730
Yahoo!

00:21:04.120 --> 00:21:05.630
We did it, didn’t we?

00:21:06.200 --> 00:21:08.910
Such a little girl is also in the newcomers’ battle...

00:21:08.910 --> 00:21:11.630
Moreover, she also chose G, did she?

00:21:13.630 --> 00:21:15.960
No. Other than her and myself,

00:21:15.960 --> 00:21:20.550
there were 14 other artisans who
had the insight to choose G.

00:21:20.550 --> 00:21:23.980
Just as expected of the people who
passed the first preliminary.

00:21:27.060 --> 00:21:27.770
To continue...

00:21:27.770 --> 00:21:32.230
The next batch of people who’ve passed are
the 13 people who chose A, or Echire butter.

00:21:32.770 --> 00:21:33.740
That’s me.

00:21:34.190 --> 00:21:38.650
I can’t call it better for making butter rolls
than the low water content butter.

00:21:38.650 --> 00:21:41.360
But that is, without a doubt, the world’s #1 butter.

00:21:41.360 --> 00:21:44.360
Those of you who picked this
also pass without complaint.

00:21:48.160 --> 00:21:51.330
Everyone’s able to properly determine the
difference between the butters, huh?

00:21:51.330 --> 00:21:54.210
Someone like me has always used goat milk butter.

00:21:54.210 --> 00:21:57.370
So, I couldn’t make out which one
was the better butter at all.

00:21:58.170 --> 00:21:59.420
Manager...

00:21:59.420 --> 00:22:02.260
I wonder if Azuma-san’s okay?

00:22:02.260 --> 00:22:04.850
I’m not worried at all.

00:22:05.680 --> 00:22:07.140
But, earlier you...

00:22:07.140 --> 00:22:08.810
The circumstances have changed.

00:22:08.810 --> 00:22:11.100
No... he changed them.

00:22:11.100 --> 00:22:13.890
What do you mean by, “the circumstances
have changed?”

00:22:13.890 --> 00:22:16.980
The trouble is whether that fool

00:22:16.980 --> 00:22:19.990
Kuroyanagi will notice “that.”

00:22:19.990 --> 00:22:21.940
What is “that?”

00:22:22.570 --> 00:22:24.120
He has...

00:22:24.120 --> 00:22:26.780
Azuma has created a miracle.

00:22:26.780 --> 00:22:30.250
By his being stuck on the de-licious
bread, his passion has...

00:22:30.250 --> 00:22:33.050
turned a difficult situation into a chance!

00:22:38.500 --> 00:22:46.640
If I think of you, and even utter the clichéd phrase “I love you,”

00:22:47.210 --> 00:22:55.650
it makes such a nice sound, and you continue talking.

00:22:59.220 --> 00:23:06.660
The hopeless tears your bold self sometimes shows me form flag of truce.

00:23:07.960 --> 00:23:11.830
If nothing is said, then all the more,

00:23:12.030 --> 00:23:17.970
I just can’t look away. Things like sadness and pain...

00:23:17.970 --> 00:23:20.540
Well, that happens a lot in life, after all.

00:23:20.770 --> 00:23:24.680
When you casually say, “Do your best,” it gives me strength.

00:23:25.120 --> 00:23:29.450
Whenever your small back trembles, I will embrace you right away.

00:23:30.480 --> 00:23:33.290
Even if the scenery outside my window changes...

00:23:33.780 --> 00:23:37.990
Stay with me as you are, bad sleeping habits and all.

00:23:38.620 --> 00:23:43.160
If you sulk, and utter

00:23:43.430 --> 00:23:51.970
Even the clichéd “I hate you,” it comes across as the opposite.

00:23:52.370 --> 00:24:01.330
I will love you, no matter what. It’s just another Sunday to me.

00:24:05.680 --> 00:24:06.840
I’m gonna win!

00:24:06.840 --> 00:24:09.010
Plucking up his courage,

00:24:09.010 --> 00:24:11.870
he kneads in a way that reminds him of his home in Aomori.

00:24:11.870 --> 00:24:14.470
So, the next Yakitate Japan is:

00:24:14.470 --> 00:24:18.530
Kazuma Disqualified!? Resurrection from the brink of death by Ultra C!

00:24:18.530 --> 00:24:19.970
Be sure to watch!

00:24:20.370 --> 00:24:22.740
Yakitate Seeds of Knowledge!!

00:24:22.740 --> 00:24:24.670
Everybody loves school lunches.

00:24:24.670 --> 00:24:27.650
By the way, I love agepan, but that’s irrelevant!

00:24:27.650 --> 00:24:31.710
Japanese school lunch was first served at Yamagata Elementary in 1890.
